    "updated_at": "2020-11-19T14:25:56Z",
    "body": "I think coupling them is fine overall. My comment there was more about layering. That proposal has to do with exceptions, not Abort signals, i.e. ignoring AbortErrors could be useful independent of AbortSignals. So just from a technical architecture point of view putting it on DOMException made more sense to me.\r\n\r\nThe OP's idea sounds good to me, and has precedent in .NET and other cancel-token using ecosystems.",
