    "updated_at": "2021-11-23T03:18:24Z",
    "body": "So the core reason for this issue has effectively been resolved by the [addition of the new `abortSignal.reason`](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1027). However that PR does give a rather nice basis for methods like `abortSignal.assertNotAborted()` in that we already have the error available.\r\n\r\ni.e. Instead of the original code in the OP we could now just have (roughly):\r\n\r\n```js\r\nAbortSignal.prototype.assertNotAborted = function() {\r\n    if (this.aborted) throw this.reason;\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
